-- ============================================================
-- Handicap history from the 2026 rounds played before the app.
--
-- Run after sql/society-handicaps.sql. Safe to run twice (rows that are
-- already there are left alone).
--
-- Those rounds were typed in as Stableford points, with no cards, so
-- each one's differential is worked out from the points: capped gross =
-- par + playing handicap + 36 - points (a blob is net double bogey), then
-- (113 / slope) x (capped gross - course rating), off the yellow tees.
-- Playing handicap = 75% of the course handicap typed in for rounds 1-5;
-- rounds 6-8 carried the index itself, so it's turned into a course
-- handicap first. Sherfield Oaks (Waterloo for round 3, Wellington for round 7),
-- Tylney Park and Downshire ratings come from published scorecards. Each row says how it was worked out.
-- These rows are history only: they change nobody's handicap by
-- themselves.
-- ============================================================

on conflict (event_id, player_id) do nothing;
